# Chrome Automation Setup

This guide explains how to configure Chrome Remote Debugging for Playwright on Windows and macOS.

---

# Windows Setup

### 1. Create Chrome Automation profile

Run PowerShell:

```powershell
$ChromePath = "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Google\Chrome\User Data"
$AutomationPath = "$env:USERPROFILE\Chrome-Automation"

New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $AutomationPath

Copy-Item "$ChromePath\Local State" "$AutomationPath\"

Copy-Item "$ChromePath\Default" "$AutomationPath\Default" -Recurse
```

### 2. Start Chrome with Remote Debugging

Run this command in PowerShell before running your Python script:

```powershell
& "C:\Program Files\Google\Chrome\Application\chrome.exe" `
--remote-debugging-port=9222 `
--user-data-dir="$env:USERPROFILE\Chrome-Automation" `
--profile-directory=Default `
--no-first-run
```

If Chrome is installed in another location, update the executable path.

---

# macOS Setup

### 1. Create Chrome Automation profile

Run Terminal:

```bash
mkdir -p "$HOME/Chrome-Automation"

cp -a "$HOME/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Local State" \
"$HOME/Chrome-Automation/"

cp -a "$HOME/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Default" \
"$HOME/Chrome-Automation/"
```

### 2. Start Chrome with Remote Debugging

Run this command in Terminal before running your Python script:

```bash
"/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome" \
--remote-debugging-port=9222 \
--user-data-dir="$HOME/Chrome-Automation" \
--profile-directory=Default \
--no-first-run
```

---

# Python Playwright Connection

After launching Chrome using the commands above, connect your Python script:

```python
from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright

with sync_playwright() as playwright:

    browser = playwright.chromium.connect_over_cdp(
        "http://127.0.0.1:9222"
    )

    context = browser.contexts[0]

    page = context.pages[0] if context.pages else context.new_page()

    page.goto("https://www.google.com")

    input("Press Enter to exit...")
```

---

# Important Notes

- Close normal Chrome before copying the existing profile.
- Chrome must be running with remote debugging before starting the Python script.
- The automation profile is a separate copy of your original Chrome profile.
- Do not run two Chrome instances using the same automation profile simultaneously.
- Keep port `9222` accessible only locally. Do not expose remote debugging to the internet.
